From 0b6db5db0534d0712798a117f81b7b54aa8f76c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:52:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add bandastation-style edge overlays for smoothed windows

Windows now draw a separately-colored frame/edging overlay on top of the
tinted glass, like bandastation's window edging:

- New client SmoothEdgeOverlay component: draws a second set of smoothed
  corner layers from an edge RSI with its own color (RESET_COLOR analog).
- IconSmooth gains an optional color field applied to the smoothed layers
  themselves, so the glass tint no longer rides on the whole sprite and
  cannot bleed into the edging overlay.
- window_edges.rsi / reinforced_window_edges.rsi: edge0-7 corner states
  extracted from the existing greyscale window art (opaque, normalized to
  white for code-side tinting).
- Window/Plasma use window_edges, Reinforced/RPlasma/Tinted use
  reinforced_window_edges, all with #4F4F4F edging; tinted windows now use
  the reinforced glass art tinted #5A6E82 like bandastation.
- Mining/clockwork/shuttle windows keep their pre-colored art: white layer
  color and overlay disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5Jv3J4u3jRYPv1wqQwaax
